    <string name="home_cost_per_km_title">What cost per km includes</string>
    <string name="home_cost_per_km_body1">The fuel or charge your kilometres used in the month, plus everything else spent on this vehicle in it (service, tolls, parking and other running costs), divided by the kilometres driven. Fuel used is an estimate: kilometres (from your odometer readings and recorded trips) times this vehicle\'s own cost per km, from its mileage and the price you paid at the time. So a month without a fill-up still has a cost per km. Swipe the card for earlier months, or tap it to see the month in Insights.</string>
    <string name="home_cost_per_km_body2">Loan EMIs and the purchase price are left out, so the number shows what it costs to run the vehicle. You can change which categories count in Settings.</string>
